WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Five meetings, one star.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.660
Here's how we draw it.

3
00:00:04.958 --> 00:00:08.615
Long before computers, Babylonian sky watchers

4
00:00:08.555 --> 00:00:12.455
knew that Venus's appearances repeated in a cycle

5
00:00:12.395 --> 00:00:13.935
of about eight years.

6
00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:18.892
Earth takes about 365 days around the Sun.

7
00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:21.332
Venus takes about 225.

8
00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:24.968
Venus catches up on the same side about every

9
00:00:24.908 --> 00:00:27.128
584 days.

10
00:00:27.948 --> 00:00:30.808
Mark 5 meetings and join them in time order.

11
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:35.207
Across this roughly eight -year cycle, a star

12
00:00:35.147 --> 00:00:35.687
appears.

13
00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:39.738
Connect their positions at equal time steps instead,

14
00:00:40.258 --> 00:00:42.978
and a different flower -like web grows.

15
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:47.357
Beautiful to look at, fun to draw, and a way to

16
00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:48.937
understand how a system works.

17
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:50.557
Try drawing it together.
